  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Go&amp;Grow &#x2013; Potato tillage and planting technologies in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Go&amp;Grow Farm Solutions (Go&amp;Grow) delivers technology, in combination with technical assistance, to growers in Africa for production of potatoes, onions, cereals, beans and pulses.Go&amp;Grow provides technical assistance in the identification, selection, procurement and financing of growing, storage and processing technology sourced mainly from Dutch manufacturers.The technology to be demonstrated comprises a set of four complementary machines for tillage and planting of potatoes:1.	An Evers tillage machine. This machine improves the permeability and drainage of the soil.2.	A Gramegna spading machine. This machine loosens, breaks and mixes the soil, as in ploughing, to reduce irrigation needs and reduce nitrogen emissions.3.	A Dewulf cultivator. This machine improves the soil structure.4.	A Dewulf belt planter. This is a new and superior alternative for the cup planting machine.This set of four machines improves the quality of the soil and the planting process, leading to higher yields and produce quality. This will be demonstrated in the project.</narrative>
  </description>
